# Everything Riparr ships runs on Linux, whichever system builds it. Git for Windows
# checks text out with CRLF by default, so the Windows runner -- which stages the
# appliance into the Windows Preparer -- would hand the box CRLF Python, CRLF systemd
# units and CRLF configs. LF in every working tree, on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts were the first to break: under Cygwin a CRLF checkout turns "pipefail"
# into "pipefail\r".
*.sh text eol=lf
